  {
    "id": "64cd27bd05bf8894b7e8",
    "source": "for a split party or a private word, and can hold the floor: soft enforcement marks who should be talking, strict actually mutes everyone else, and a raised-hand queue keeps it civil. A table can also opt into rules that make the call behave like the world: proximity hearing (you only hear players whose characters are near yours on the map, while the GM hears everyone), whisper and shout ranges, walls muffling speech, and downed characters going deaf. All of that lives under Live voice chat in the Settings tab, and all of it is off by default, so a plain group call is what you get until the table asks for more.",
    "sourceHash": "64cd27bd05bf8894b7e8c7e6a05b292f0115784e1d985fd3fa4f0a67c584e917",
    "kinds": [
